    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "While 義務 (gimu) can translate to 'responsibility' in the sense of 'duty' or 'obligation', the English lemma 'responsibility' is broader, also encompassing 'accountability' and the 'burden/charge' of a task. 義務 is therefore a narrower term, covering only a subset of the English meaning. The most natural and comprehensive Japanese equivalent for the general concept of 'responsibility' is 責任 (sekinin).",
